# SIH IPsec Correlation Layer

Implementation workspace for the Expected-vs-Observed Correlation Layer of the
SIH IPsec Security Assessment Framework.

- **Phase 1** — Discovery: `PHASE_1_DISCOVERY_REPORT.md` (read-only; the SIH
  repository `D:\sihipsec` was only inspected).
- **Phase 2** — Canonical data contract: `correlation/` package + `tests/`.
- **Phase 3** — Real expected-state materialization: `correlation/adapters/`
  (read-only extraction from `D:\sihipsec` artifacts), CLI in `correlation/tools/`,
  reports `PHASE_3_VARIABLE_TRACEABILITY.md` + `PHASE_3_EXPECTED_STATE_REPORT.md`.
- **Phase 4** — Deterministic Expected-vs-Observed Comparison Engine:
  `correlation/comparison/`, reports `PHASE_4_COMPARISON_ENGINE_REPORT.md` +
  `PHASE_4_COMPARISON_MATRIX.md`.
- **Phase 5** — ML integration layer (adapter-only, deterministic test double):
  `correlation/ml/` + `correlation/comparison/ml_comparison.py`, reports
  `PHASE_5_ML_INTEGRATION_REPORT.md` + `PHASE_5_ML_FEATURE_CONTRACT.md`. No
  external ML dependencies; no real trained model exists in `D:\sihipsec`.
- **Phase 6** — Risk assessment & scoring: `correlation/risk/`, reports
  `PHASE_6_RISK_ENGINE_REPORT.md` + `PHASE_6_RISK_RULE_TRACEABILITY.md`.
- **Phase 7** — XAI explainability layer: `correlation/xai/`, reports
  `PHASE_7_XAI_REPORT.md` + `PHASE_7_XAI_TRACEABILITY.md`.
- **Phase 8** — Read-only Security Analyst Dashboard: stdlib `correlation/api/`
  (adapters + store + routes + `http.server` app) + `dashboard/` (Vite + React
  + TypeScript strict + Tailwind + Recharts), 9 pages, deterministic snapshot
  export (`out/dashboard_snapshot.json`). Reports `PHASE_8_DASHBOARD_REPORT.md`
  + `PHASE_8_UI_DATA_MAPPING.md`.
- **Phase 9** — Deterministic Response & Policy Enforcement layer:
  `correlation/response/` (models, policy, rules, authorization, approval,
  audit ledger with SHA-256 chain, dry-run executor, planner, engine),
  reports `PHASE_9_RESPONSE_REPORT.md` +
  `PHASE_9_RESPONSE_RULE_TRACEABILITY.md`. Dry-run only, approval for
  high-impact actions, UNKNOWN becomes review/capture, NOT_APPLICABLE becomes
  no response. Later phases: PCAP download API, Kafka/streaming, production
  executors (Phase 10), real ML training & serving.
- **Phase 10** — Production Operations & Live Streaming:
  `correlation/streaming/` (schema, topics, partitioning, dedup, backpressure,
  DLQ, retries, offsets, windowing, live adapter, ML provider, pipeline),
  `correlation/execution/` (settings, targets, idempotency, host, executors,
  gates), `correlation/api/` v1 + live context + PCAP download, and
  `correlation/config.py` + `.example.env`. Two-layer gateway: only an approved
  + authorized Phase-9 recommendation may be executed, production OFF by
  default, DRY_RUN never has a network effect. Reports:
  `PHASE_10_PRODUCTION_REPORT.md`, `PHASE_10_ARCHITECTURE.md`,
  `PHASE_10_STREAM_SCHEMA.md`, `PHASE_10_EXECUTION_POLICY.md`,
  `PHASE_10_DEPLOYMENT.md`, `PHASE_10_TEST_REPORT.md`.

## Constraints

- `D:\sihipsec` is the source/reference repository and is NEVER modified from
  this workspace.
- All implementation lives under `D:\sihcolayer`.
- Python 3.10, standard library only (no runtime dependencies).
- Serialization: object -> dict -> JSON (JSON-compatible primitives; never
  `pickle`).

## Package layout

```text
correlation/
    version.py              correlation_schema_version = "v1"
    models/
        identity.py         CorrelationIdentity
        expected.py         ExpectedState (IkeExpected / EspExpected / TrafficExpected)
        observed.py         ObservedState / SpiObservation / TransitionObservation
        features.py         LiveFeatureWindow (feature_schema_version="v2")
        ml.py               MLResult (contract only; no ML)
        evidence.py         EvidenceRef
        observability.py    Observability / OBSERVABILITY / TRACEABILITY metadata
        correlation.py      CorrelationInput / CorrelationResult
    comparison/
        clock.py            Clock domains + explicit ClockAlignment
        discrepancy.py      ComparisonOutcome + status constants
        rules.py            Deterministic per-variable comparison rules
        engine.py           ComparisonEngine + identity safety + aggregation
        ml_comparison.py    Expected-vs-ML outcomes (source=ml, never in
                            Protocol mismatch lists; ML_TRAFFIC_CLASSIFICATION,
                            ML_ANOMALY)
    ml/
        feature_contract.py Canonical v2 59-feature contract snapshot + validators
        model_metadata.py   ModelMetadata provenance (version/dataset/labels)
        models.py           Deterministic nearest-centroid demo/test-double model
        training.py         Reproducible training + JSON artifact I/O library
        adapter.py          Raw model output -> canonical traffic profile mapping
        inference.py        Feature window -> MLResult (traffic_class/confidence/anomaly)
        integration.py      Attach ML outcomes to CorrelationResult.metadata["ml"]
    risk/
        models.py           RiskFinding / RiskAssessment, severity & source vocab
        policy.py           Versioned RiskPolicy (weights, bands, caps, toggles)
        findings.py         Deterministic finding construction + deduplication
        rules.py            Deterministic risk rules + RULE_TRACEABILITY registry
        scoring.py          Score aggregation + severity-band mapping
        engine.py           RiskEngine.assess orchestration + identity safety
    xai/
        models.py           ExplainabilityResult + nested explanation models
        templates.py        Deterministic phrasing + XAI_TRACEABILITY registry
        explainers.py       Finding + ML explanation build (read-only)
        evidence.py         Evidence preservation (exact, dedup, sorted)
        score_explanation.py  Score explication (consumed, never recomputed)
        engine.py           ExplainabilityEngine.explain orchestration
    response/
        models.py           Finite actions/statuses/roles/priorities + domain
                            models (recommendation, plan, approval, authz,
                            execution, audit event) + state machine + hashing
        policy.py           Versioned ResponsePolicy (gates, ML cap, expiry)
        rules.py            RESPONSE_RULE_TRACEABILITY registry
        authorization.py    Role capability checks -> AuthorizationDecision
        approval.py         Analyst approval gate (PENDING/APPROVED/REJECTED/
                            EXPIRED)
        audit.py            Append-only SHA-256 chained audit ledger
        executor.py         DryRunExecutor (network_effect ALWAYS False)
        planner.py          Deterministic ResponsePlan from Phase 4-7 outputs
        engine.py           ResponseEngine state-machine lifecycle
    streaming/
        models.py           StreamEvent + event_identity (SHA-256 canonical)
        schema.py           stream-schema-v1 registry + JSONL validation
        topics.py           topic routing (sih.live.*, dead-letter)
        partitioning.py     deterministic partitioning by identity
        dedup.py            LRU-stream dedup (idempotent redelivery)
        backpressure.py     ACCEPT/BUFFER/BLOCK/DROP/DLQ flow control
        dlq.py              dead-letter (preserves original payload)
        retry.py            bounded exponential backoff
        offsets.py          batched commit + checkpoint + rewind
        producer.py         StreamProducer (fan-out plugins)
        consumer.py         StreamConsumer (per-partition, in-order)
        config.py           StreamingConfig (window/lookback/from_env)
        windowing.py        WindowEngine (100 ms, frontier, gap-fill)
        live_adapter.py     XdpEventAdapter + UDP/4500 NAT-T classification
        ml_provider.py      MLInferenceProvider (unavailable/real/test-double)
        pipeline.py         ContinuousPipeline (Phase 4->6->7->9 -> events)
    execution/
        base.py             ExecutorBase + DECISION status vocabulary
        targets.py          ExecutionTarget (typed; key() for idempotency)
        settings.py         ExecutionSettings (DRY_RUN default; production OFF)
        idempotency.py      IdempotencyRegistry (bounded, replay-safe)
        host.py             HostOperations + UnavailableHost (fail-closed)
        executors.py        Xdp/Firewall/StrongSwan executors (structured ops)
        gates.py            ExecutionControlPlane (gateway in order)
    api/
        store.py            phase-8 lib/store/evidence read-only handlers
        routes.py           phase-8 contract for /api/lib/* and /api/health
        app.py              http.server DashboardServer (+ --phase10 v1 wiring)
        v1.py               /api/v1 health/metrics/traffic-generator/evidence
        live.py             Phase10Context + TrafficGeneratorMonitor
        pcap.py             PcapRegistry/PcapService (root-hardened)
    config.py               ProductionConfig.from_env + .example.env template
    observability/
        health.py           HealthRegistry (healthy/degraded/unavailable/disabled)
        metrics.py          Phase10Metrics.collect_all + Prometheus text
    schemas/
        json_schema.py      JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) documentation
    adapters/
        expected_state.py   ExpectedStateAdapter: real expected-state materialization
                            from plan.json / campaign JSON / metadata / config
    tools/
        materialize_expected.py  CLI (single + --batch JSONL)
tests/                      unittest suite + fixtures (marked TEST FIXTURE)
out/                        materialization output (JSONL batch), regenerated
```

## Quick start

```bash
cd D:\sihcolayer
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

```python
from correlation.models import CorrelationInput, CorrelationIdentity

inp = CorrelationInput.from_dict({...})   # canonical serialized shape
payload = inp.to_json()                   # object -> JSON
back = CorrelationInput.from_json(payload)  # round trip
```

## Phase 3 — materialize real expected state

```bash
# one sample (full JSON to stdout)
python -m correlation.tools.materialize_expected --plan <path-to>plan.json --sequence 1

# batch: every plan sample as JSONL (default out\expected_states.jsonl)
python -m correlation.tools.materialize_expected --plan <path-to>plan.json --batch

# campaign / explicit-config routes
python -m correlation.tools.materialize_expected --campaign campaign-quality.json --sequence 1
python -m correlation.tools.materialize_expected --config config.json --run-id run-01 --sequence 1
```

Reads ONLY from `D:\sihipsec` artifacts; never writes there. `run_id` is
inferred from a plan path of the form `results/datasets/<run_id>/staging/plan.json`.
Reports: `PHASE_3_VARIABLE_TRACEABILITY.md`, `PHASE_3_EXPECTED_STATE_REPORT.md`.

## Phase 4 — deterministic comparison engine

```python
from correlation.adapters import ExpectedStateAdapter
from correlation.comparison import ComparisonEngine, ComparisonEngineOptions
from correlation.models import ObservedState

materialized = ExpectedStateAdapter().from_plan(r"tests\fixtures\datasets\dataset-20260916-231246\staging\plan.json", sequence=1)

engine = ComparisonEngine(ComparisonEngineOptions())
result = engine.compare(
    materialized,                     # ExpectedState or MaterializedExpectedState
    ObservedState(timestamp_ns=1_500_000_000, endpoints={"a": "192.0.2.1", "b": "192.0.2.2"},
                  tunnel_seen=True, ike_seen=True, esp_seen=True),
    observed_identity=materialized.identity,
    observed_values={...},            # authoritative audit/swanctl evidence (optional)
)
result.status   # MATCH | MISMATCH | UNKNOWN | NOT_APPLICABLE
```

Conservative by design: crypto variables are UNKNOWN unless authoritative
observed values are supplied (audit/swanctl channel); `capture_filter`,
`configuration_id`, `security_posture` compress to NOT_APPLICABLE; absence
results in MISMATCH only when the live window is COMPLETE. From Phase 5 the
engine also records `ml_evaluated` when an `MLResult` is supplied (the engine
itself never makes ML a mismatch; ML outcomes live under `metadata["ml"]`).
Reports: `PHASE_4_COMPARISON_ENGINE_REPORT.md`,
`PHASE_4_COMPARISON_MATRIX.md`.

## Phase 5 — ML integration (adapter-only, deterministic)

`D:\sihipsec` contains NO trained model (verified: stdlib-only feature
pipeline, no sklearn/joblib/pickle artifacts). Phase 5 therefore provides a
documented deterministic test-double (z-scored nearest centroid, stdlib-only)
so the full ML contract is exercised end-to-end, plus a model-agnostic adapter
so a real externally-trained model substitutes directly.

```python
from correlation.comparison import ComparisonEngine
from correlation.ml import (load_artifact, train_nearest_centroid,
                            correlate_with_ml, save_artifact)
from correlation.models import LiveFeatureWindow

model = train_nearest_centroid(rows, model_version="v0-demo",
                               training_dataset="...", estimate_confidence=True)
save_artifact(model, r"tests\fixtures\ml\centroid-demo-v0.json")
model = load_artifact(r"tests\fixtures\ml\centroid-demo-v0.json")

window = LiveFeatureWindow(window_start_ns=0, window_end_ns=1_000,
                           features=features)   # MUST be the canonical v2 59

engine = ComparisonEngine()
result = correlate_with_ml(engine, expected, observed,
                           identity=..., observed_identity=...,
                           model=model, window=window,
                           ml_result=None)      # or precomputed MLResult
result.metadata["ml"]       # provenance + Expected-vs-ML comparisons
result.metadata["ml_evaluated"]
```

Rules: feature schema is exactly v2 / the authoritative 59 names; missing,
extra, renamed, non-numeric, NaN/inf features fail fast (never filled);
confidence is only set when the model provides probabilities; the anomaly seam
stays `None` when the model has no anomaly capability; ML outcomes are
recorded under `metadata["ml"]` with `source="ml"` and NEVER enter
`matches`/`mismatches`/`unknowns` or the overall status; ML output never
becomes a risk/severity conclusion. Reports: `PHASE_5_ML_INTEGRATION_REPORT.md`,
`PHASE_5_ML_FEATURE_CONTRACT.md`.

## Phase 6 — Risk Assessment & Security Scoring

Deterministic read-only engine consuming Phases 3-5 outputs:

```python
from correlation.risk import RiskEngine, RiskPolicy
from correlation.models import MLResult

engine = RiskEngine(RiskPolicy.default())          # risk-policy-v1
assessment = engine.assess(expected=expected,      # ExpectedState | MaterializedExpectedState
                           observed=observed,      # ObservedState (optional)
                           correlation=result,     # Phase-4 CorrelationResult
                           ml_result=ml,           # Phase-5 MLResult (optional)
                           evidence_refs=refs)     # EvidenceRef[] (optional)
assessment.overall_score   # bounded 0-100
assessment.severity        # INFO | LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
assessment.findings        # RiskFinding[] (deduplicated, rule-tagged)
assessment.identity        # CorrelationIdentity (safety-checked)
```

Rules derive from the authoritative SIH posture model (`posture_of_config` in
`D:\sihipsec\controller\dataset_planner.py`, read-only): PFS-off and CBC
family are MEDIUM(12), `modp2048` with PFS on is LOW(6); IKE is a fixed
baseline (never graded); AES-128 is never a weakness. UNKNOWN/NOT_APPLICABLE
never become vulnerabilities; ML evidence is capped at LOW; no finding is
CRITICAL alone (CRITICAL is the aggregate band >= 40 across categories).
Reports: `PHASE_6_RISK_ENGINE_REPORT.md`, `PHASE_6_RISK_RULE_TRACEABILITY.md`.

## Phase 7 — XAI / Explainability layer

Deterministic read-only layer converting Phase-4 comparison results, Phase-5
ML results, and Phase-6 risk assessments into structured, traceable
explanations. It explains existing decisions only: it never creates a finding,
never changes a score/severity, never recomputes risk, and never fabricates
evidence.

```python
from correlation.risk import RiskEngine, RiskPolicy
from correlation.xai import ExplainabilityEngine

assessment = RiskEngine(RiskPolicy.default()).assess(expected=expected,
                                                     correlation=result,
                                                     ml_result=ml)

xai = ExplainabilityEngine().explain(assessment,   # RiskAssessment (required)
                                     correlation=result,   # optional enrichment
                                     ml_result=ml)         # optional enrichment
xai.score_explanation      # score/severity/policy consumed verbatim from assessment
xai.finding_explanations   # why_it_was_flagged (rule templates + generic fallback)
xai.ml_explanations        # classification + anomaly (model-derived evidence only)
xai.unknown_explanations   # UNKNOWN -> evidence gap (never MISMATCH/vulnerability)
xai.not_applicable_explanations
xai.evidence_summary       # exact refs, deduped/sorted; fabricated is always False
```

Runs with the stdlib on Python 3.10; no model imports (explains existing ML
metadata). Reports: `PHASE_7_XAI_REPORT.md`, `PHASE_7_XAI_TRACEABILITY.md`.

## Phase 8 — Security Analyst Dashboard (read-only)

Read-only visualization of the Phase 3–7 outputs. Backend is a zero-dependency
stdlib service; every value it serves comes from the already-computed Phase
4/5/6/7 results (adapter = pure view-model mapping, no re-decisioning):

```bash
# 1) serve API + built dashboard (build output lives in dashboard/build)
python -m correlation.api.app            # http://127.0.0.1:8000

# 2) lib/api/<id>/, /api/assessments, /api/health (+ 404/405 codes)
# 3) dev (proxy /api -> 127.0.0.1:8000): cd dashboard && npm install && npm run dev

# regenerate the deterministic snapshot used by the no-backend demo mode
python -m correlation.tools.execute_phase8 --out out/dashboard_snapshot.json
cp out/dashboard_snapshot.json dashboard/public/dashboard-snapshot.json

# dashboard build + checks
cd dashboard && npm run typecheck && npm run test && npm run build
```

The dashboard renders backend outputs verbatim: no frontend scoring, no color-
only status, `UNKNOWN`/`NOT_APPLICABLE` preserved, ML labeled model-derived
(`traffic-rf-v1-demo`), evidence paths text-only, XAI text as text. Without
`VITE_API_BASE_URL` the app reads `dashboard/public/dashboard-snapshot.json`, so
the UI runs with no backend. Reports: `PHASE_8_DASHBOARD_REPORT.md`,
`PHASE_8_UI_DATA_MAPPING.md`.

## Phase 9 — Response & Policy Enforcement (dry-run)

Deterministic, controlled, auditable response RECOMMENDATIONS built from the
Phase-6 risk assessment (plus optional Phase-4 correlation / Phase-5 ML /
Phase-7 XAI). The layer NEVER executes a real network operation, never
auto-blocks, and records every lifecycle step in an append-only SHA-256-chained
audit ledger.

```python
from correlation.response import ResponseEngine, ResponsePolicy
from correlation.response.authorization import auth_context

eng = ResponseEngine(policy=ResponsePolicy.default(), clock=demo_clock)  # injected clock
plan = eng.plan(assessment)          # RiskAssessment (required) -> ResponsePlan

rec = plan.by_id()["RR-RISK-PFS-DISABLED"]
approval = eng.request_approval(rec, "analyst-1", reason="proceed")
eng.approve(approval, rec, "analyst-1", roles=("ANALYST",))
eng.authorize(rec, auth_context("operator-1", ("SECURITY_OPERATOR",)))
result, rec = eng.execute_dry_run(rec, auth_context("operator-1", ("SECURITY_OPERATOR",)), "operator-1")
result.network_effect      # ALWAYS False in Phase 9
eng.ledger.verify()        # SHA-256 chain integrity

# high-impact/unknown/terminal handling
eng.cancel(rec, "operator-1")          # CANCELLED
eng.expire(plan)                       # EXPIRED (injected clock only)
```

Safety invariants: severity alone never maps to a blocking action (max is
REQUIRE_REVIEW); high-impact actions are approval+authorization gated and
dry-run only; ML-derived findings are capped at REQUIRE_REVIEW and never block;
UNKNOWN evidence gaps become CAPTURE_EVIDENCE (never MISMATCH/vulnerability);
NOT_APPLICABLE produces no response. Reports:
`PHASE_9_RESPONSE_REPORT.md`, `PHASE_9_RESPONSE_RULE_TRACEABILITY.md`.

## Phase 10 — Production Operations & Live Streaming

Controlled, observable, deterministic live pipeline on top of Phase 9:

```bash
# full regression
python -m unittest discover -s tests          # 762 OK (1 symlink skip)

# run the dashboard with the live Phase-10 context attached
python -m correlation.api.app --phase10       # http://127.0.0.1:8000

# /api/v1 surface (read-only)
GET /api/v1/health            # component states + overall
GET /api/v1/metrics           # Prometheus text exposure
GET /api/v1/traffic-generator # status (UNKNOWN until a feed is seen)
GET /api/v1/evidence/{id}     # evidence metadata (ID-based)
GET /api/v1/evidence/{id}/pcap  # binary PCAP download (.pcap/.pcapng)
```

```python
from correlation.streaming.pipeline import ContinuousPipeline
from correlation.execution import ExecutionControlPlane, ExecutionSettings

# streaming: XdpEventAdapter -> WindowEngine -> MLInferenceProvider ->
#            ContinuousPipeline.process(record).to_events(source)
# enforcement: two-layer gateway only executes an APPROVED + AUTHORIZED
#              Phase-9 recommendation, in order:
#               recommendation -> authorization -> approval -> idempotency
#               -> expiry -> executor (mode + allow-list + host)
cfg = ProductionConfig.from_env()   # DRY_RUN by default; production OFF
cfg2 = ProductionConfig.from_env({"SIHEXEC_MODE": "production"})  # raises
                                  # without SIHEXEC_ENABLE_PRODUCTION_EXECUTION
```

Safety invariants (asserted in tests): production starts OFF; DRY_RUN has
`network_effect=False`; ML verdicts never reach enforcement directly; typed
operations only — no shell/SSH strings; SUCCEEDED is only reported when the
injected host confirms `applied=True`; executions are idempotent and mirrored
into the Phase-9 SHA-256 audit chain. Reports: `PHASE_10_PRODUCTION_REPORT.md`,
`PHASE_10_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PHASE_10_STREAM_SCHEMA.md`,
`PHASE_10_EXECUTION_POLICY.md`, `PHASE_10_DEPLOYMENT.md`,
`PHASE_10_TEST_REPORT.md`.

## NOT implemented (outside the Phase 1–10 scope)

Real model training on captures & production ML serving, real Kafka brokers /
production swanctl daemons, and fabrication of the live XDP sensor into this
workspace. The Phase 1–8 scope, the Phase 9 deterministic response layer, and
the Phase 10 streaming + controlled execution gateway are complete.